From: 6ixtyn9-sudo <270680834+6ixtyn9-sudo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 06:51:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] enhancement lane: floor gate, autobets lifecycle, floor
 replay (stages 2-4)

Stage 2 - gate by hit rate and a price floor, no EV veto
  Operator ruling: "betting on ev will lead us to not bet at all, we have the
  track record of enhanced, we know what wins more, we just need prices above a
  certain threshold, like how autobets does it."
  ENHANCEMENT_PRICE_FLOORS (src/edgefactory/enh_registry.py) starts at
  match_over_25 1.60, match_over_15 1.45, match_over_35 3.30, btts_yes 1.85;
  floors are re-derivable from the settled registry (audit_recent_picks.py
  --track-record prints rate, breakeven 1/rate, floor and profit per market and
  per bucket/rule slice). Below the floor there is no bet - not paper, not
  shadow. clears_floor is strict about what "is a price" (no bools, strings,
  NaN, inf or <= 1.0) and False for any market with no floor, so a floorless
  market can never fire: the team unders that used to print a bet line no
  longer do. enhancement_breakeven / enhancement_edge_sample stay on the row as
  information and gate nothing. The board and the slip call the same
  clears_floor, so they cannot disagree; the board's line is now
  picks_today.enhancement_board_line (bet line unchanged above the floor,
  explicit refusal below it). Everything is percentages of capital.

Stage 3 - presentation and lifecycle identical to autobets, additive
  Operator ruling: "i need it to look like how autobets presents it and to have
  the same lifecycle of autobets" / "i dont want them to change the system have
  now ... additional". scripts/auto_tickets.py is parameterised by
  Lane{state_file, slip_prefix, label, stake_frac}; the enhancement lane keeps
  its own state (localdata/enhancement_tickets_state.json) and artifact
  (localdata/enhancement_tickets_<date>.txt) and re-uses the existing freeze,
  settlement, bank (bank += ret_pct - staked_pct) and take-profit
  (cycle_base x2) code paths rather than growing lookalikes. Gated by
  EDGE_FACTORY_ENH_BOARD=1; unset restores today's behaviour verbatim.

Stage 4 - replay_harness --enhancements
  Replays settled registry records against floor= variants, reporting hit rate
  and mean log growth per bet-day (the harness's primary metric, not final
  bank) with the existing small-n flag; --ab reuses the paired day-bootstrap
  already in the harness. It prints its own limit: it can only replay history
  that had a price.

Stage 1 - not built, and reported as such
  Pricing enhancements from the schema-2 detail ledger needs the Stage 0
  capture work, which is not in this clone: betexplorer_match_detail appears
  nowhere in the tree or in any git history, and the only nearby schema writer
  (_write_fixture_cache) writes schema 1. Loading prices out of a schema nobody
  here has seen would be guessing at field names, so the join is left out
  rather than faked.

Also fixes a state-path leak found while landing Stage 3: MAIN_LANE held
STATE_FILE as a value, so tests (and any tool redirecting that global) wrote
into localdata/auto_tickets_state.json - 811 lines of real state were truncated
in this workspace before it was caught. Lane state paths resolve through
state_path() at call time now, and the leak is pinned by a regression test.

Tests: PYTHONPATH=src .venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q -p no:randomly
2771 passed.

