Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 07:12:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] enablement: --enhancements without the flag is a no-op,
 and stage the daily-run wiring

Found while preparing the operator's enablement step (the step passes
`--enhancements`; the flag gates the lane).

* `auto_tickets.py --enhancements` with EDGE_FACTORY_ENH_BOARD unset used to fall
  through to the MAIN lane and print the AUTO TICKETS status block - a step
  labelled "enhancement tickets" would report the main lane's performance and
  imply the lane was live while it was off. It now says the lane is disabled and
  changes nothing (no state read, no artifact). Pinned by a test that fails if
  the main lane is touched from that path.
* docs/operator/enhancement-lane.yml.proposed: today's daily.yml with exactly two
  hunks - the EDGE_FACTORY_ENH_BOARD env flag and a `--enhancements` step after
  the smart schedule (advisory, continue-on-error). Nothing else in the repo runs
  the lane, so the env var alone is inert; that is why the invocation is part of
  the proposed change. YAML parses; one step added, none removed or renamed.

Not pushed: PR #61 stays as reviewed. This commit is for the follow-up branch
after #61 merges.

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
